        "results_interpretation": "The pooled effect size of 0.98 suggests a relationship between omega-3 fatty acids and breast cancer incidence; however, the 95% confidence interval of (0.77, 1.25) includes the null value of 1, indicating that the exposure is not associated with the disease. Furthermore, the high heterogeneity value (I\u00b2 = 83.95%) points to substantial variability among the included studies, which raises concerns about the consistency of the findings. This variability may reflect differences in study populations, methodologies, or measurements of omega-3 fatty acid intake. Overall, the evidence does not support a definitive link between omega-3 fatty acids and breast cancer incidence based on the current analysis."
